Every member of the Police Department shall conduct himself or herself in a proper and law-abiding manner at all times and shall avoid the use of unnecessary force. Prohibited conduct shall include, but not be limited to, the following:
(1) Absence from regular hours of duty without permission;
(2) Sleeping or loafing on duty;
(3) Insubordination or disobedience of orders;
(4) Engaging in any games of chance;
(5) Drinking any intoxicating beverage while on duty or in uniform;
(6) Willful maltreatment of any person or prisoner;
(7) Using violent, profane or insolent language;
(8) Acting in a disorderly, immoral or any other manner as to bring discredit upon the Department;
(9) Giving out or releasing any information covering the affairs, business or operation of the Police Department or the City without the consent of the Police Chief or City Council;
(10) Receiving or accepting a reward from any person, firm or corporation for any services rendered in the line of duty;
(11) Accepting bribes of money, gifts, or other articles of apparent or actual value, or accepting any fee, reward or gift of any kind from a person arrested or from any friend on his behalf while he is in custody or after his release or discharge;
(12) Active participation in any political campaign to the neglect of his official duty;
(13) Making an arrest for an act growing out of a personal argument on the part of the officer or any member of his family;
(14) Engaging in any practice that tends to or does lure the public into violations of the law.
(Prior Code, § 14-8; Code 2004, § 46-7)

