The following words, terms and phrases, when used in this chapter, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:
Manufactured/mobile home.
(1) The term "manufactured/mobile home" means a factory-built dwelling unit built on a permanent chassis and made to be readily transportable on its own running gear in one or more sections totaling no less than 576 square feet which is subject to the Georgia Motor Vehicle Title Registration Act (O.C.G.A. § 40-2-1 et seq.) and meeting the construction and safety standards of the national code administered by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development. The term "manufactured/mobile home" does not include recreational vehicles. Every manufactured/mobile home shall:
a. Be suitable for year-round occupancy;
b. Be placed on a permanent masonry foundation or other substantial foundation that will comply with the Georgia Mandatory Building Code for the erection and support of manufactured/mobile homes and to be substantially fixed to its site also in compliance with the Georgia Mandatory Building Code;
c. Be connected to a water system approved by either the City, or the State Department of Natural Resources, Environmental Protection Division, as the case may be, and present to the City Inspector a letter or certification of such approval;
d. Be connected to an approved waste disposal system approved by either the City, or the State Department of Natural Resources, Environmental Protection Division, as the case may be, and present to the City Inspector a letter or certification of such approval;
e. Have all electrical supply systems and connections that comply with the current Georgia Mandatory Electric Code; and
f. Be landscaped with trees, shrubs, and other plant material substantially equal to or better than one-family dwelling within 500 feet.
(2) The area between the bottom perimeter of the manufactured/mobile home and the ground shall be covered with material that is suitable and adequately functional to adequately protect the underside of the manufactured/mobile home and to keep the manufactured/mobile home from being unsightly. The owner of the manufactured/mobile home is responsible for the skirting.
Manufactured/mobile home park.
(1) The term "manufactured/mobile home park" means a parcel of land which has been planned and improved for the placement of two or more manufactured/mobile homes for nontransient use and occupancy or for rental occupancy. A conditional use permit shall be required for the establishment of a manufactured/mobile home park. The term "park" includes the term "community."
(2) The owner of a tract or parcel of land who has placed a manufactured/mobile home on that tract or parcel of land as his residence may place one additional manufactured/mobile home on the tract of land, as long as the second manufactured/mobile home is not rented and the two manufactured/mobile homes located on the tract of land shall not be classified as a manufactured/mobile home park.
Manufactured/mobile home space means a plot of ground within a manufactured/mobile home park designated for the accommodation of not more than one manufactured/mobile home of single-family occupancy.
Modular home.
(1) The term "modular home" means a factory-fabricated transportable building consisting of building units designed to be incorporated at a building site on a permanent foundation as a permanent structure with the appearance of a conventional on-site constructed building and to be used for residential purposes. A modular home is not a manufactured/mobile home. The term "modular home" shall include the terms "manufactured home" and "prefabricated home." Every modular home shall:
a. Be suitable for year-round occupancy;
b. Be placed on a permanent masonry foundation or other substantial foundation that will comply with the Georgia Mandatory Building Code for the creation and support of manufactured/mobile homes and to be substantially fixed to its site also in compliance with the Georgia Mandatory Building Code;
c. Be connected to a water system approved by either the City, or the State Department of Natural Resources, Environmental Protection Division, as the case may be, and present to the City Inspector a letter or certification of such approval;
d. Be connected to an approved waste disposal system approved by either the City, or the State Department of Natural Resources, Environmental Protection Division, as the case may be, and present to the City Inspector a letter or certification of such approval;
e. Have all electrical supply systems and connections that comply with the current Georgia Mandatory Electric Code;
f. Be landscaped with trees, shrubs, and other plan material substantially equal to or better than one-family dwelling within 500 feet; and
g. Meet the general construction and safety standards of the latest edition of the Georgia Mandatory Building Code.
(2) The area between the bottom perimeter of the manufactured/mobile home and the ground shall be covered with material that is suitable and adequately functional to adequately protect the underside of the manufactured/mobile home and to keep the manufactured/mobile home from being unsightly. The owner of the manufactured/mobile home is responsible for the skirting.
Rent or rental means any remuneration, whether in money, barter, or kind, that is given or received as consideration for the occupancy of a manufactured/mobile home or the occupancy of a tract, space or parcel of land upon which a manufactured/mobile home is situated.
Service building means a building housing facilities such as recreational, maintenance, laundry, and office structures necessary to the successful development and management of a manufactured/mobile home park.
Travel trailer means a motorized camper, converted bus, tent-trailer or other similar vehicular or portable structure used or designed for temporary portable housing or occupancy while on vacation, recreational, or other trip and provided with sleeping accommodations. The travel trailer shall not be used for permanent housing or permanent residence.
(Code 2004, § 50-2)

